Z||000005||RossT||01-26-2001||11:33 PM||||If you take the window sticker off, it destroys the value of the car....<P>so what all does Barc. have left to sell?<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 01-26-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||01-27-2001||12:34 AM||||I guess I'm screwed......the window sticker is gone!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Barc isn't in a big selling mood.......too many people not following through with any deals.  He has had several inquiries and I have fielded several myself and nothing materialized.  He has traded a bunch of Fieros lately (mostly '85 GTs) and now has a large collection of late model Camaros & Trans-Ams (about 6 or 7 of each) & BMW's (plus some Vettes & '67 Firebird convertibles).<P>At any rate, he plans on keeping the Fieros he has (at least for the forseeable future).  They include:<P>-'87 GT, silver/gray, 5-sp., 9800 miles.<P>-'85 GT black/gray, 4-sp., 33K miles.<P>-'85 GT bright red/gray, 4-sp., T-Tops 34K miles.<P>-'87 SE burgundy/gray, 5-sp., T-Tops, 36K miles<P>-'87 SE black/gray, 5-sp., 44K miles<P>-'88 Formula burgundy/gray, 5-sp., 1333 miles<P>-'88 Formula, burgundy/gray, 5-sp., T-Tops, 232.8 miles<P>-'88 Formula, burgundy/gray, 5-sp., T-Tops, 114.1 miles<P>-'88 Formula, bright red/gray, 5-sp., T-Tops, 38K miles<P><BR>That's it!  He used to have over 50 Fieros, so you can see that he pared down his collection quite a bit.  I have personally bought 3 Fieros from him......my 16K mile black '88 GT (had 10K miles on it when I bought it), my 281 mile silver Formula and a 44K mile yellow Formula that I regrettably sold last year (I miss that car!).<P>RossT bought his red '88 GT T-Top from him too and Tim P. bought his 117 mile '88 GT from him too, so at least 5 have found good homes!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>I think he would consider selling his remaining Fieros if someone made a serious offer and wasn't just kicking tires.  If anyone is interested e-mail me and we'll talk.||||reg||6
Z||000007||rodmcneill||01-27-2001||12:41 AM||||Mrfiero, pardon my ignorance, but who is Barc? Where does he get all these low mileage Fiero's and where is he located?||||reg||5
Z||000008||Haze_Performance||01-27-2001||12:43 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by mrfiero:<BR><B><P>-'88 Formula, bright red/gray, 5-sp., T-Tops, 38K miles<P>I think he would consider selling his remaining Fieros if someone made a serious offer and wasn't just kicking tires.  If anyone is interested e-mail me and we'll talk.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hmmm.... do you think $5000 is a good offer? <BR>I would love that car.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/ttttttt.gif">  <BR><B>"AHHHHH!!!!!!!!!!! All Fiero's don't start on fire you BONEHEAD!!!!"</B><p>[This message has been edited by Haze_Performance (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||7
Z||000009||mrfiero||01-27-2001||12:51 AM||||rod,<P>Barc is the owner of these beautiful Fieros and is in the Denver area.  He started buying them in '87 (the silver '87 GT was his first Fiero).  He fell in love with them and just started buying any and all (as long as they had the V-6 and manual tranny).  He especially liked the '85 GT and '88 Formula and at one time owned about 15 of each.  <P>Ross knows him because he bought his GT from him......sorry for the confusion.<P><BR>Haze,<P>I don't think he would go that low......I believe he was looking for $7500 or so.  A lot of $$, but it is gorgeous (ask RossT).<p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000010||RossT||01-27-2001||09:14 AM||||I have seen most of these cars, and while some may have some dust on them, they are worth the asking price.  Cars with simular miles on them go for much much more on autotrader.com.  All of his cars are stored inside. My car took some detailing, and fluid exchanges, but looks and runs like day 1, and no leaking.<BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003403.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum1/HTML/003403.html</A> <P>Ross<p>[This message has been edited by RossT (edited 01-27-2001).]||||reg||1
